From: Genesis builder <builder@genesis.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:35:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] B20_R1 H01 + Repair A: reproduce the four B20 review
 findings; globally disjoint research/evaluation material

- audit/review_b20/reproduce_b20_review.py: read-only reproduction of B20-REVIEW-01..04 from
  stored evidence (no prover); findings.json records exact slots, rows and source hashes.
- learning/partitions.py: one partition builder for the whole study. All research-visible
  material is frozen into an exposure set first; evaluation material is drawn against it
  with EXACT / ALPHA / INSTANCE / GENERALIZES relations, cross-unit distinctness,
  quarantine, and an explicit INSUFFICIENT_DISTINCT_MATERIAL failure. InsertionScreen
  covers lemma, macro, memory, curriculum and import routes with ALLOW/BLOCK only, a
  salted commitment and a query budget. partition_problems is a pure validator.
- tests_formal/test_learning_partitions.py (15 tests): the original four slots are
  detected; cross-seed, alpha and instance collisions rejected; tampering and changed
  exposure detected; no reserved text leaks.

Does not sanitize the B20 comparison: that observation stays contaminated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
